@startuml
' Evidence: src/experiences/mylibrary/MyLibrary.tsx (addToReadingList, startReading, moveSelectedToCompleted, saveReview, removeSelected)
' Evidence: src/experiences/mylibrary/MyLibrary.tsx (visitorLibrary and visitorReviews)
' Evidence: src/experiences/mylibrary/types.ts (CuratedLibraryState and BookReview)
!include _theme.iuml

title Personal-book lifecycle in the current visit

state "Outside My Library" as Outside
state "Reading list" as ReadingList
state "Currently reading" as Current
state "Completion review\n(not yet committed)" as CompletionReview
state "Completed with review" as CompletedReviewed
state "Completed without review\n(visitor fixture only)" as CompletedUnreviewed
state "Review editor" as ReviewEditor
state "Removed" as Removed

[*] --> Outside
Outside --> ReadingList : owner adds from catalogue
ReadingList --> Current : Start reading
Current --> ReadingList : owner starts another book\n/ previous current returns to list
ReadingList --> CompletionReview : Move to completed
Current --> CompletionReview : Move to completed
CompletionReview --> ReadingList : cancel [origin was list]
CompletionReview --> Current : cancel [origin was current]
CompletionReview --> CompletedReviewed : save valid rating\n/ move and store review
CompletedReviewed --> ReviewEditor : Edit review
ReviewEditor --> CompletedReviewed : save or cancel
ReadingList --> Removed : Remove
Current --> Removed : Remove
CompletedReviewed --> Removed : Remove / delete review
CompletedUnreviewed --> Removed : Remove

state "Visitor fixture creation" as VisitorFixture
VisitorFixture --> CompletedReviewed : deterministic reviewed entries
VisitorFixture --> CompletedUnreviewed : every third completed entry
VisitorFixture --> Current
VisitorFixture --> ReadingList

note bottom of CompletionReview
  Rating 1..5 is required.
  Comment is optional and limited to
  500 characters by the current UI.
end note

note bottom
  These are serial-number memberships in React state,
  not persisted records or server-side workflow states.
end note
@enduml
